WEBVTT

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:10.000
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.470
Ogata shot me at Abashiri.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:16.130
Wilk, too.

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.550
And it was Kiroranke who gave the signal.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.500
Inkarmat saw it.

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:25.040
Ogata said the same thing.

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:29.080
But until we hear from 
Kiroranke Nispa directly...

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:34.430
Inkarmat supposedly asked 
Kiroranke why he killed Wilk.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:40.650
Kiroranke said something 
about how he'd changed.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:45.720
How he was supposed to go tell their 
old comrades the location of the gold.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:52.900
I trusted him from the bottom 
of my heart. And loved him.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.450
What you did to Wilk...

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:00.900
Was that why Sofia was mad?

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:03.910
Sofia may know everything!

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.390
Damn you!

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:26.810
You'll pay for what you did to my men!

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:21.260
Lieutenant Koito...

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:24.920
Don't do anything.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:27.150
I'll finish him.

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:46.140
Tanigaki, shoot!

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:53.190
Wait!

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:54.860
Asirpa!

00:02:58.320 --> 00:02:59.780
I need to ask him something.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:01.240
Don't shoot!

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:03.780
Move! He's a wounded beast!

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.160
Get away from us!

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.150
If you kill him, I'll never know the answer!

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:09.910
We're running away, Asirpa.

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:14.410
Stories about Wilk and Sofia...

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:19.320
The key must be inside you...

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:45.530
We're running away, Asirpa.

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:48.090
Kiro-chan...

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:52.040
You can't stay here.

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:54.180
Run.

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:57.360
The key is inside you.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:03:59.630
The key...

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:02.720
I remembered everything a moment ago.

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:06.010
It was something Aca told me after all.

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:10.980
Thank you for helping me remember.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.050
What are they talking about?

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:14.950
Oh...

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:18.730
I see.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:22.760
I'm glad...

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:26.990
This journey wasn't for nothing.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:32.740
I didn't bring you all the way here

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:36.750
for nothing.

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:39.750
No...

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:42.990
We did do a lot of pointless things.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:03.400
It's in your hands now, Asirpa.

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:08.740
For us... Go with Sofia.

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:26.090
Sofia!

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:41.860
Is it true that you killed Aca?

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.220
Kiroranke Nispa!

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:51.000
Kiroranke Nispa!

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:55.620
Kiroranke Nispa...

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:12.390
This ice is made from water 
that freezes in the Amur River.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:15.320
Kiro-chan told me that.

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:22.680
When summer comes, the ice will melt, 
and he can rest in the water of his homeland.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:33.030
Kiro-chan just took everything too seriously!

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:45.430
Why did Aca have to die?

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.480
I wanted to hear from him directly.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:55.030
Was it because he killed the 
Ainu and stole their gold?

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:56.860
Asirpa-san...

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:04.310
Just before he was shot, he told me that 
he wasn't the one who killed the Ainu.

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:07.030
Really?

00:07:10.510 --> 00:07:12.320
Oh, right! Sofia!

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:14.230
Where did she go?

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:15.830
She should be close!

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:19.030
Tsukishima!

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:20.830
Are you okay?

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:22.060
I'm fine.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:24.320
He's a mess.

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:26.050
We're heading back to Ako now.

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:27.710
Tanigaki, can you carry him?

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:28.670
Yes!

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:29.430
Huh?

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:32.930
Isn't that the girl from the lighthouse?

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:36.350
There's someone over there, too!

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:37.890
You're Asirpa, right?

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:40.660
We came all the way here to find you.

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:43.310
Sugimoto made a deal to help us.

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:45.810
Don't leave us without my permission.

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:47.070
I'll go take a look!

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:48.200
Me, too!

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:00.230
They're fighting.

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:13.500
More! More!

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:21.060
Is that you, Sugimoto-san?

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:22.780
What a coincidence.

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:24.280
I didn't see anything, did you?

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:33.840
It's dangerous to try and 
enter the country by boat.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:37.410
We both went north by the same route, huh?

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:47.400
Farewell, Kiroranke.

00:08:56.620 --> 00:09:00.560
Once we take them to Ako, 
should we go look for Sofia?

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:03.880
No, I'll see Sofia again.

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.080
She'll come look for me.

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:08.470
Yeah.

00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:10.070
Oh, Asirpa-san...

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:12.360
You can have this back.

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:20.370
Thank you, Sugimoto.

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:27.720
Let's head back to Hokkaido, Asirpa-san.

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:44.330
Farewell, kiddo...

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:46.800
I won't forget you.

00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:04.040
<b>Episode Thirty-Six
To Live</b>

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:07.040
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:13.050
<b>Ako: Nivkh Village</b>

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:22.930
Just like Enonoka's people, 
the Nivkh keep lots of dogs, huh?

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:26.680
Their clothes are similar to the Uilta.

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:31.630
We're a little different, 
and a little bit the same.

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:33.930
I never would've learned that in Hokkaido.

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:48.960
Why was Ogata working with Kiroranke?

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:53.870
I can't see him caring about 
ethnic minority independence.

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:57.800
Does he really just want the gold?

00:10:58.120 --> 00:10:59.910
I hope so.

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:03.130
That would make it easier to kill him.

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:07.680
Svetlana...

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:14.500
I understand why you would 
want to leave the island.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:19.320
And why your parents would 
want to know you're okay...

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:25.220
Follow Gansoku to Russia.

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:31.310
But make sure you write a letter. 
I'll deliver it on my way back.

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:37.730
As long as they know you're alive, 
they can get out of that black pit.

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:42.700
All right. I promise.

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:51.480
I'm going to make it rich in St. Petersburg.

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:55.920
I'll get rich and bring my 
parents to live with me!

00:11:57.130 --> 00:12:00.970
<i>Gansoku and Svetlana would, 
for some unknown reason,</i>

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:04.010
<i>go on to have great adventures 
on the continent.</i>

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:07.560
<i>But that's a story for another time.</i>

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:13.770
There's a traditional Nivkh 
dish that uses fish skin.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:16.160
She'll make it for us, she says.

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:17.070
Fish skin?

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:21.370
They strip off the fish skin, 
stew it, roll it up and smash it.

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:26.140
They mix in lingonberries and black 
crowberries, and flavor it with seal fat.

00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:28.840
Then they put it outside 
to cool, and it's done.

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:30.800
It's a snack you can only eat in winter.

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:32.060
They call it mosu.

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:33.310
Mosu!

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:39.820
It's yummy. It tastes like kanten.

00:12:40.970 --> 00:12:41.980
Mosu!

00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:45.820
You're in a good mood, Lieutenant Koito.

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:48.580
I just remembered my father.

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:49.830
Mosu.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:55.250
We got Asirpa back. 
We succeeded in our mission.

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:57.950
I'm happy I get to report that to my father.

00:12:58.850 --> 00:13:01.140
He should be proud.

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:04.800
I'm sure Lieutenant Tsurumi will be, too.

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:08.160
Eat up, Tsukishima!

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:10.810
Get better soon so we 
can go back to Hokkaido!

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:16.560
What kind of meal is that?

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:19.310
It's not food. It's a dressing for wounds.

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:22.580
There's white mugwort that 
grows along the coasts.

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:25.820
The Nivkh all put it on 
their wounds to heal them.

00:13:31.190 --> 00:13:35.410
But she says the herbs alone can't heal him.

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:38.420
We need to bring a doctor here.

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:40.260
An Ako doctor?

00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:43.240
We're Japanese soldiers here illegally.

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:45.170
What if he calls the police?

00:13:45.710 --> 00:13:49.680
There's no need to risk 
our lives to save Ogata.

00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:54.950
But we need to get Sergeant Tsukishima 
looked at by a real doctor, right?

00:13:57.450 --> 00:14:00.440
If we all dress as Nivkh, 
nobody will notice, right?

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:03.840
Russians can't tell the 
difference between us.

00:14:10.590 --> 00:14:12.800
I'm full. I can't take any more patients.

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:15.450
He says he's too busy.

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:18.680
Tell him to please come 
because lives are at risk.

00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:23.060
Koito will pay lots of money.

00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:24.360
Japanese?

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.610
I fought in the Russo-Japanese War.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:33.170
If we don't have to hide, 
that makes this faster.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.100
You Japanese soldiers?

00:14:42.750 --> 00:14:46.480
We came to get back a kidnapped girl.

00:14:47.010 --> 00:14:51.340
Once we're better, we're going back to Japan.

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:58.750
He's badly hurt. I need to operate 
someplace cleaner, or he'll die.

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:01.730
We need to take him to my hospital.

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:04.840
He says the hospital has better equipment.

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:07.130
No. Do it here.

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:09.720
You want to save him, right?!

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:15.010
Fine. Let's take him there.

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:18.250
Sugimoto, you can't...

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:20.760
I've got lots of questions for Ogata.

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:22.860
He can't die yet.

00:15:31.020 --> 00:15:33.050
He says if he sells us out to the Russians,

00:15:33.050 --> 00:15:36.620
he'll have wasted his time saving his life.

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:44.630
You're not dumb enough to think that

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:49.130
Ogata's going to get better and tell 
you everything you want to know, right?

00:15:50.310 --> 00:15:52.470
It's not him I want to save.

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:22.160
I've done all I can.

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:25.670
But his breathing and 
blood pressure are dropping.

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:28.670
He won't last till morning.

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:31.210
He says he'll die soon.

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:39.340
What do we do?

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:41.500
Make sure he's dead.

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:45.120
Sugimoto?

00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:51.500
I'll see if there's no way to save him.

00:17:11.750 --> 00:17:12.960
Ogata fled!

00:17:13.480 --> 00:17:16.630
Asirpa-san! Ogata fled!

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:21.930
Get around to the back! Shiraishi and 
Tanigaki, head over there to look!

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:23.430
He can't have gone far!

00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:26.480
Stay close, Asirpa-san!

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:31.510
Are you alive?

00:17:31.510 --> 00:17:32.570
Hang in there.

00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:37.160
B-Behind...

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:45.460
Knock him out!

00:17:46.180 --> 00:17:47.230
Russian?

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:48.960
Or I'll kill the girl!

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:01.600
Rich fool.

00:18:09.300 --> 00:18:12.400
Genjiro-chan, look at this!

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:13.530
What is it?

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:15.980
Are these Ogata's footprints?

00:18:15.980 --> 00:18:17.530
No, they're yours.

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:19.210
Let's look over there.

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:34.460
Ogata's going to get away!

00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:37.340
Are you going to shoot?

00:18:37.790 --> 00:18:39.130
I'll aim for the horse!

00:19:08.890 --> 00:19:13.790
<i>Come back when you feel 
all better, so I can kill you.</i>

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:21.400
Are you just going to go
 back to Lieutenant Tsurumi?

00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:22.730
Yeah.

00:19:22.730 --> 00:19:28.870
They only need you until 
they've cracked the code.

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:31.270
They'll be keeping a tight watch on you,

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:33.400
but it'll be safer than being 
with Hijikata Toshizou.

00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:35.000
Why?

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:40.700
Didn't Aca entrust me with the gold so 
I could work with Hijikata Toshizou?

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:45.280
Did he tell you something?

00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:52.930
I trained Asirpa to hide in the mountains
and fight like a guerrilla.

00:19:52.930 --> 00:19:56.500
She'll be the one to lead the Ainu.

00:19:57.670 --> 00:19:59.250
No, nothing.

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:04.610
Finding the gold might lead 
us to who killed the Ainu,

00:20:04.610 --> 00:20:06.970
and what happened to Aca.

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:10.390
It might fill in the blanks 
we don't have answers to yet.

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:13.770
What will you do, Sugimoto?

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:18.520
Keep working with 
Lieutenant Tsurumi to find the gold?

00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:24.530
I've asked for a share of the gold 
in exchange for my cooperation.

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:30.370
It was the only way I could 
think of to find you again,

00:20:31.550 --> 00:20:36.420
and tell you what happened 
that night at Abashiri Prison.

00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:38.550
I see.

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:41.240
I'm not taking their orders,

00:20:41.240 --> 00:20:46.510
but they took all the skins, and Lieutenant 
Tsurumi is the one closest to the gold.

00:20:46.960 --> 00:20:49.220
First, we'll find it.

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:52.200
So you do need money.

00:20:53.280 --> 00:20:53.960
Yeah.

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:58.520
Then we're still on the same road together.

00:21:00.810 --> 00:21:01.720
Yeah.

00:21:06.610 --> 00:21:08.450
Sugimoto!

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:10.520
We're ready!

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:12.200
We're ready to go whenever!

00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:13.420
Right!

00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:17.130
Asirpa-san!

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:23.970
I'm renewing our contract as partners.

00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:27.190
Yeah.

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:54.500
<i>Yeah, I need money.</i>

00:21:55.700 --> 00:21:59.000
<i>But there's something 
just as important to me.</i>

00:22:00.800 --> 00:22:03.500
<i>I'll find the gold and 
put an end to all this!</i>

00:22:04.490 --> 00:22:09.070
<i>And free Asirpa-san from this war for it!</i>
